\ A `once` word defined inside a module, read from an importing file.
\
\ This is the path the top-level fixtures leave uncovered. The cell's body resolves bare words
\ against its own module, and the only thing carrying that module across the freeze is the stamp
\ the image loader writes from the row's `module_name`. A force that read the executing
\ visibility instead would resolve against *this* file and find neither the `private{ }` helper
\ nor the module-level binding.
\
\ The body also contains a `;`, so the row's `may_define` bit has to survive too: without it the
\ definition lands in whatever frame happened to be on top rather than a transient one.

use "support/once_module_state.1z" ;

body-runs .  \ 0  -- nothing runs until the word is referenced
scaled .     \ 40 -- the private helper and the binding both resolved
scaled .     \ 40 -- reused
body-runs .  \ 1  -- one body entry across both reads
